---
#1824: `t.app` declares its own `Repo` beside a `uses` of `t.core`, whose
`Repo` `t.model`'s `Run` names. The shadow is legal, and so is every use here:
`retag` moves a `t.core` `Repo` from one imported position (`first`'s result)
straight into another (`Run.repo`), and the rest touch only `Run.n` and the
local `Repo`. Neither `Repo` ever meets the other.
---
commons t.app

uses t.core
uses t.model

type Repo = Int

fn retag(r: Run) -> Run {
  Run { repo: first(r), n: r.n + 1 }
}

fn size(r: Run) -> Int {
  r.n
}

fn mine() -> Repo {
  7
}
